diagnostics/python-habits-operators.em:2:19: a condition must be a Bool, but this is Int
  if choice == 1 or 2 {
                    ^
`2` is a value, not a comparison. Write the comparison again for each value: `choice == 1 or choice == 2`.
diagnostics/python-habits-operators.em:5:7: multiplication needs numbers, but this is String and Int
  print("-" * 20)
        ^^^^^^^^
To repeat text, write `"-".repeat(20)`.
diagnostics/python-habits-operators.em:7:13: subtraction needs numbers, but this is String and String
  var clean = word - "!"
              ^^^^^^^^^^
To take text off the end, write `word.remove_suffix("!")`. `remove_prefix` takes it off the start.
diagnostics/python-habits-operators.em:9:7: remainder needs numbers, but this is String and String
  print("Hello %s" % name)
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Emerald has no `%` formatting. Put the value in the text with interpolation: `"Hello #{name}"`.
diagnostics/python-habits-operators.em:13:13: addition needs numbers, but this is Nothing and Int
  var total = add(2, 3) + 1
              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
`add` gives back nothing, because it declares no result. Give it a result type and `return` the value instead of printing it.
diagnostics/python-habits-operators.em:15:10: addition needs numbers, but this is List[Int] and Int
  scores = scores + 3
           ^^^^^^^^^^
To add an item to a list, write `scores.append(3)` on its own line; it changes the list. To make a new list instead, write `scores.chain([3])`.
